ely, and prospective credit opinions. Built on a foundation of independent thinking, rigorous analytics, and an open and balanced approach towards credit research, Ind-Ra has grown rapidly during the past decade, gaining significant market presence in India's fixed income market.</p>\r\n<p>Ind-Ra currently maintains coverage of corporate issuers, financial institutions (including banks and insurance companies), finance companies, urban local bodies, and structured finance and project finance companies.</p>\r\n<p>Headquartered in Mumbai, Ind-Ra has seven branch offices located in Ahmedabad, Bengaluru, Chennai, Gurugram, Hyderabad, Kolkata, and Pune. Ind-Ra is recognised by the Securities and Exchange Board of India and the Reserve Bank of India.</p>\r\n<p>Ind-Ra is a 100% owned subsidiary of the Fitch Group.</p>","industry":"Road Assets–Toll |  Annuity |  Hybrid-Annuity","industryName":null,"isRACPriority":false,"fileName":null,"isAWCTriggerCompleted":true,"isRACMailSent":true,"racMailSentDateTime":"0001-01-01T00:00:00","primaryAnalyst":null,"priority":null,"primaryAnalystName":"Nikhil Joshi","primaryAnalystDesignation":"Senior Analyst","primaryAnalystCompanyName":"India Ratings and Research Pvt Ltd","primaryAnalystAddress":"Wockhardt Towers, 4th Floor, West Wing, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra East,Mumbai - 400051","primaryAnalystContactNumber":"02240356155","secondaryAnalystName":"Nikhil Joshi","secondaryAnalystDesignation":"Senior Analyst","secondaryAnalystCompanyName":null,"secondaryAnalystContactNumber":"02240356155","tertiaryAnalystName":null,"tertiaryAnalystDesignation":null,"tertiaryAnalystCompanyName":null,"tertiaryAnalystContactNumber":null,"additionalAnalystName":null,"additionalAnalystDesignation":null,"additionalAnalystCompanyName":null,"additionalAnalystContactNumber":null,"chairpersonName":"Abhash Sharma","chairpersonDesignation":"Director","chairpersonCompanyName":null,"chairpersonContactNumber":"9999999","mediaRelationName":"Ankur Dahiya","mediaRelatio